## Why This Is Asked
Introduces a grid-path DP with a bounded number of teleports, forcing state compression and a 2D prefix max to keep complexity at O(KRC). It tests correctness, backtracking, and memory considerations beyond standard path DP.

## Key Concepts
- DP on grid with at most k teleports
- 2D prefix max to propagate bestPrev for teleport transitions
- Reconstruction: store choice or re-run DP with pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxEnergy(grid, k) {
  const R = grid.length, C = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  let dpPrev = Array.from({length:R}, () => Array(C).fill(NEG));
  dpPrev[0][0] = grid[0][0];
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    const bestPrev = Array.from({length:R}, () => Array(C).fill(NEG));
    for (let r = 0; r < R; r++) {
      for (let c = 0; c < C; c++) {
        bestPrev[r][c] = dpPrev[r][c];
        if (r > 0) bestPrev[r][c] = Math.max(bestPrev[r][c], bestPrev[r-1][c]);
        if (c > 0) bestPrev[r][c] = Math.max(bestPrev[r][c], bestPrev[r][c-1]);
      }
    }
    const dpCurr = Array.from({length:R}, () => Array(C).fill(NEG));
    for (let r = 0; r < R; r++) {
      for (let c = 0; c < C; c++) {
        if (r === 0 && c === 0) continue;
        let best = NEG;
        if (r > 0) best = Math.max(best, dpCurr[r-1][c]);
        if (c > 0) best = Math.max(best, dpCurr[r][c-1]);
        if (bestPrev[r][c] !== NEG) best = Math.max(best, bestPrev[r][c]);
        if (best !== NEG) dpCurr[r][c] = best + grid[r][c];
      }
    }
    dpPrev = dpCurr;
  }
  return dpPrev[R-1][C-1];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What is the time/space complexity and how would you optimize for very large grids?
- How would you implement robust path reconstruction for the teleport usages?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a fresh DP angle: interval-based value depends on distinct characters within each substring, plus precise reconstruction for k blocks.

## Key Concepts

- Non-overlapping interval DP
- Precomputing distinct counts for all substrings
- Reconstruction via back-pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch
function maxKSubstrings(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dist = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const freq = new Array(26).fill(0);
    let setBits = 0;
    for (let j = i; j >= 0; j--) {
      const idx = s.charCodeAt(j) - 97;
      if (freq[idx]++ === 0) setBits++;
      dist[j][i] = setBits;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  const start = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][0] = 0;
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      // Option 1: skip i
      if (dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
        prev[i][t] = i-1;
        start[i][t] = start[i-1][t];
      }

      // Option 2: end t-th substring at i
      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const val = dp[s-1][t-1] + dist[s-1][i-1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = s-1;
          start[i][t] = s-1;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct substrings
  const result = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (prev[i][t] === i-1) {
      i--;
    } else {
      result.unshift([start[i][t]+1, i]);
      i = prev[i][t];
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { maxValue: dp[n][k], substrings: result };
}
```

Time complexity: O(n²k) for DP transitions + O(n²) for preprocessing. Space: O(n² + nk). Optimizations include limiting the inner loop or using convex hull tricks for special cases.

## Why This Problem Matters
This problem assesses sophisticated dynamic programming techniques by combining palindrome preprocessing, optimal substructure for non-overlapping segment selection, and explicit solution reconstruction. It integrates preprocessing with suffix-based DP while requiring careful index management.

## Key Concepts
- Palindrome table (isPal) DP preprocessing for O(1) palindrome queries
- 2D DP with optimal substructure and complete solution reconstruction
- Complexity analysis: Time O(n²k), Space O(n² + nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPalBlocks(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const isPal = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(false));

  // Precompute palindrome table
  for (let len = 1; len <= n; len++) {
    for (let l = 0; l + len <= n; l++) {
      const r = l + len - 1;
      isPal[l][r] = (s[l] === s[r] && (len <= 2 || isPal[l+1][r-1]));
    }
  }

  // Initialize DP tables
  const dp = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  const trace = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(null));

  // Fill DP table
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i + 1][t];
      trace[i][t] = {type: 'skip'};

      for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
        if (isPal[i][j]) {
          const val = (j - i + 1) + dp[j + 1][t - 1];
          if (val > dp[i][t]) {
            dp[i][t] = val;
            trace[i][t] = {type: 'take', l: i, r: j};
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let i = 0, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i < n) {
    const choice = trace[i][t];
    if (choice.type === 'take') {
      blocks.push([choice.l, choice.r]);
      i = choice.r + 1;
      t--;
    } else {
      i++;
    }
  }

  return {maxLength: dp[0][k], blocks};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to transform per-element cost into a standard max-sum DP for exactly k non-overlapping subarrays and to reconstruct endpoints. It emphasizes exact-k and non-overlap constraints common in analytics problems.

## Key Concepts
- Transform to B[i] = A[i] - c and reduce to max-sum of k non-overlapping subarrays
- DP states: local[i][t] for subarray ending at i; glob[i][t] for best so far with t subarrays
- Recurrences and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(B, k) {
  const n = B.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const local = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const glob  = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  local[0][0] = 0; glob[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      local[i][t] = Math.max(local[i-1][t] + B[i-1], glob[i-1][t-1] + B[i-1]);
      glob[i][t] = Math.max(glob[i-1][t], local[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return {max: glob[n][k], endpoints: []};
}
```

